      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-21123",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Given a decoupled system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066958/assets/17657d7db880fc0ababc24511039a9d7446952f7521e31ae3351adbb6b28ee61.png)\nthe formula for the general solution is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066958/assets/44a286f1a4c15598038f38cdb4140534bac24caacb36f32ee4ef9cbe05b3e5e1.png)\n\nFirst, we write our differential equation in matrix form:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066958/assets/d9b9ac7fc20d076110f99476fc48d3c00c4206dc37fb2a929893fcbbb77d6526.png)\n\nSince the matrix of the differential system is diagonal, the system is decoupled. \n\nTherefore, the general solution is given by\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066958/assets/4f7cfa979200fccf811a7e0d9a633b7919b33b7740c635a921b75ad09995e700.png)",
          "category": "ma_capture",
